WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.968
-Oh, my God.
You know what I forgot?

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.067
-What did -- What did you --

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.267
-I forgot how bouncy
these chairs were.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.968
Every time I'm here,
I always remember.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.667
-Are they bouncy?
-They are so bouncy.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:10.968
-I've never really sat in them.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.367
Well, let me try.
Do you want to sit in my chair?

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:13.501
-Yeah.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:14.834
-Yeah, you can sit here --
-I would love to.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.033
Let me see if this --
how bouncy this is.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.968
Ooh, yeah.
Pretty bouncy.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:19.968
Yeah, you're right.
-Whoa.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:20.968
-How's it feel?

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.300
-Feels great to be Jimmy.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.968
[ Laughter ]
-It feels great to be Noah.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.334
How -- how you doing, bud?
-I'm doing good.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.367
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.000
[ Laughter ]
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.100
Look at this great crowd.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.133
I love these guys.
-Wow.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.934
-Um...

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.300
I heard -- I heard you're going
to school in the fall.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.067
-I am. I'm going to college.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.167
-Wow. Good for you, bud.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:42.834
Now, was that always the plan?
-Are we doing a switch?

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.067
Or am I staying here?

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.133
-Yeah, you can do the switch
if you want, yeah.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.067
-All right. Go back.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.467
[ Laughter ]
What?

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.234
-Yeah, why not? This -- we'll
keep switching chairs

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:51.234
the whole thing.
-Okay.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.467
-Where are you going to school?

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.467
-I'm going to
the University of Pennsylvania.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yo! Good for you.
-Yeah. Very exciting.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.000
-What are you majoring in?
What are you studying?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.701
-I'm majoring in business
and entrepreneurship.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.834
So -- yeah, so I'll be minoring
in like, film,

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.267
and taking film classes,
of course. I have to.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.868
-You've done film, yeah, so --
-Yeah.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.267
-You might study yourself.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.267
[ Laughter ]
That'd be amazing.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.567
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah, imagine

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.701
if you're studying yourself.
-That would be crazy.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.100
-But that's pretty fun.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.133
-Yeah, and I'd just love to
learn about, like,

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.334
building businesses.

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:21.367
And I just recently launched
a product.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.834
-What products
have you launched?

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:27.267
-It's called TBH. It's like
a healthy Nutella kind of thing.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.200
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, I love Nutella,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.367
but it's -- it's bad for you,
so I made it healthy.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.100
-So you made a healthy Nutella.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.100
-Are you gonna -- are --
you live on campus?

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.234
-So, yeah.
So I have a roommate.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.834
And I -- that's one thing I was
actually very excited about,

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.934
was -- was having --
living in a dorm.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.534
Like, what is that like?

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.400
-Does -- Does your roommate know
that it's you

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.434
moving in with him?

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.267
-Yeah. Yeah. We -- We talked.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.501
And he's, like --
he's cool about it. Yeah.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:52.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.901
-I mean, he's going to be
the most popular kid in school.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.434
-Really?
-Yes, of course.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.033
I mean, dude, you're
Noah Schnapp, come on.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.901
-Okay. I mean, it -- we're --
he -- his like, parents know

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.367
my parents and everything.
So it's, like...

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:05.100
-You know, I -- I follow you
on all the socials.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.367
I know you're on the Instagram,
you're on Twitter.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.033
You have 20 million on each one.
@NoahSchnapp.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.367
He's a good follow, by the way.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.334
And you said that TikTok
is your favorite app.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:15.968
-Yeah. I feel like it's just
the most, like, authentic.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.267
Like, you can be the most real.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:21.000
It's just not -- Instagram's
so fake, I feel like.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.968
And I -- I just, I love how
funny and authentic TikTok is.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.868
And there's actually a debate
going on, on TikTok.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:28.868
-Okay.
-Have you heard about

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.000
the wheels or doors?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.167
-Oh, yeah.
-Have you guys heard about this?

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.601
-Audience: Yeah!

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.167
-All right, so there's a debate.
What -- What is it now, again?

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:38.300
-So -- So, someone created
this debate, if --

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.667
whether there's more doors
or wheels in the world.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.467
What -- what is your stance
before I -- before I make my --

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.434
-Are there more doors or wheels?

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.634
-Just, in the entire world.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:52.033
-Well, I'm much older than you,
Noah.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:54.200
I've lived a long life,
and I will tell you that...

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.834
-Okay.
-There are more wheels

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.300
than there are doors.
-Okay, team wheels.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.534
Me, too.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.234
-Wait, you're team wheels?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:02.400
-Right?
-I feel like -- I just --

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.033
I think if you just think
about suitcases and strollers

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:09.701
and cars, trucks --
-Suitcases and strollers.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.534
-I'm ready to fight anyone
who says doors.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.100
-Wow! All right.
This is very good.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.033
We're team wheels.
-Yeah, I'm glad we agree.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:17.868
-Never forget, buddy.
Team wheels, yeah.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:20.501
-I'm just saying.
I'm team, like -- I mean, yo.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.334
-No.
-You're talking about doors

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.434
versus wheels, I mean.

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.601
-No! Kick -- Get him out.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.200
-Now, listen -- find me --
Let's just take a building.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.601
Like, okay --
-Okay, but a building,

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:33.067
think about every --
every office has a --

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.300
Every -- there's office chairs.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.467
They all have five wheels
on them.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:36.934
-Not all of them.
Not all of them.

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:37.968
But every --
-Then they have six wheels!

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.501
-Every -- Every office
has doors.

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.133
-And every office
has office chairs.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:44.000
And think about cars.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.567
Think about --
-Every car has doors.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.267
Every car has doors.
-This is out of control.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.400
-Tariq, most doors --
-Absolutely not.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.834
-Most doors have handles.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.567
And on those handles are wheels.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.400
-Get out of here!
-Think about conveyor belts.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:58.234
Yes, Jimmy.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.667
Boo!

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.701
-We -- We've got to count it up,
man.

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.834
Tally -- Tally --
-I -- I want to talk about

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.367
"Stranger Things"
before you leave, okay?

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.801
"Stranger Things" season four.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.267
I know you can't give away
any spoilers.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.267
Everyone's so excited
about this thing.

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:15.267
Congrats.
-Thank you.

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:16.367
-You're great.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.100
I know they're coming back
for season five,

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.100
and they're kind of wrapping
it up in season five.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.701
-Oh, my God. I mean,
they just --

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:25.167
they recently posted this letter
that they wrote,

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.567
which I never saw
until they post it.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.033
'Cause they don't really tell us
anything.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.467
'Cause they know I'm --
I'm always spoiling stuff.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.367
So, they -- they -- they put out
this letter,

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.200
and it was like,
"The show's ending, that's it.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.434
This is the beginning
of the end."

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.467
And I read it
and I was just bawling.

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:38.801
I was so upset.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.200
And I texted Millie --
my castmate, who plays Eleven.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.467
-Of course.
-And she was like --

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:43.667
she was like,
"You're crying too?"

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.267
Like, "So am I."
And then she texted Gaten,

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:47.534
who also plays Dustin,
and he was like,

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.834
"I'm crying too."
And then we all texted

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.734
The Duffers and we were like,
"This is so sad.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.067
Like, I can't believe
this is over."

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.501
And they were like, "You guys
gotta stop texting us.

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:57.567
Like, I -- I know it's over,
but -- but we have time left."

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.067
But it's --
-Yeah, and they started crying.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.334
[ Laughter ]
-They were crying.

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:01.567
-Were they -- yeah.
-I mean, I --

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.934
-'Cause that was your whole
childhood, really.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.534
-It's crazy.
I mean, I grew up on the show.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.167
-You did.
-I -- I've been on it --

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:07.868
I auditioned for it
when I was 9.

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.234
I'm now, like,
turning 18 this year.

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:10.901
-That's wild, buddy, right?
-Yeah, so --

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.734
-That's gonna be insane.
-It's -- It's --

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.667
-Well, you did a great job,
and everyone does a great job

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.701
on there, buddy.
And -- and you too, yeah.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:19.234
Before you cry, come back,
and we'll --

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:20.300
we'll talk about the show more.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.767
It's not over, it's not over.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:22.934
-Okay, you're right, you're
right. We have one more season.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:25.300
-If you could do this for me,
though --

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.934
in one word,
could you describe season four?

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.734
-I would say chaos.

00:05:29.734 --> 00:05:31.601
Complete and utter chaos.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.934
I would say it -- it's
everywhere and has everything

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.734
and doesn't miss a beat.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:38.567
-'Cause it looks like everyone's
in different spots.

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.667
-Everyone's spread out
everywhere.

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:43.501
It's -- It's just the craziest,
biggest thing

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:44.667
you've seen
from "Stranger Things."

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.567
-I will take that.
Noah Schnapp everybody!

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.767
One of our pals.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:50.100
Volume one of "Stranger Things"
season four

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.100
begins streaming May 27th.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.300
We'll be right back with a
performance from Nilufer Yanya.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.434
Stick around everybody.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.734
-♪ 4 and 3 and 2 and 1 ♪

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:02.167
♪ See them shots when they hear
the boot scoot and turn ♪

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.901
♪ Down with my fellow,
Questlove and y'all ♪

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:07.167
♪ I got more rhymes than
Fab Freddy got paint ♪

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:09.300
♪ Got rhymes that's rough
and some rhymes that's nasty ♪

